Subject: [PATCH] [REQ-185] Restore REQ-174's fixed fixtures for the two
 timeline probes (Route A)

Implements: do-work/working/REQ-185-restore-fixed-timeline-probe-fixtures.md

The first repair in UR-039 that was dropped wholesale with no supersession
component. Every anchor 9cf9008 touched was found in its exact pre-REQ-174 state, so
all six hunks were restorable and all six are restored.

- timelineFixedFixturePayloadScript: REQ-FIXED-DONE completed at the range start,
  REQ-FIXED-OPEN still running at the fixed now, range 2026-06-01 to 2026-08-31T12:00Z
  with now at the range end, projection.queueEnd empty
- Installed in the load handler of both the trailing-window and Now/Fit-all probes,
  before the first Timeline render
- boardNowMs reads payload.timeline.now instead of re-reading the global
- Landing probe filters on REQ-FIXED-DONE instead of the live REQ-164
- Both Go-side comments describing the step regime as live-queue-dependent replaced
  with REQ-174's text stating the fixture pins the refusal regime
- REQ-174's lessons-do-kanban.md entry restored

Kept REQ-174's D-03 (the unreachable enabled branch stays): REQ-177 is the queued
request that revisits that choice, and pre-empting it here would leave it nothing to do
and drop refusal coverage it must retain.

The lessons entry is restored in meaning, not bytes: its link named a different
repository and omitted the UR-037/ path segment, so a verbatim restore would have
re-introduced a dead link.

Both probes green in a real browser (2.05s, 2.17s); maintainer-check ALL GREEN with the
strict browser lane at 67.6s.

Unblocks REQ-177, whose requirements name timelineFixedFixturePayloadScript directly.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

UR-039 consolidates into do-work/archive/UR-039/ with this REQ, its last member.
